  "issue": {
    "id": "I_kwDOCBF7SM8AAAABOGnmpg",
    "databaseId": 5241431718,
    "number": 6398,
    "title": "Theta* generatePath skips expanding the last popped node (false no-path)",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/issues/6398",
    "body": "## Summary\n\n`ThetaStar::generatePath` expands `curr_data` **before** popping the next node from the open set. The loop condition is `!queue_.empty()`.\n\nAfter the last remaining node is popped, the queue is empty, so the loop exits **without**:\n\n1. calling `setNeighbors` on that node\n2. checking `isGoal` on that node\n\nIf that node is the only 8-connected gateway out of a pocket, or is the goal itself, planning returns failure even though a collision-free grid path exists.\n\nThis is independent of `how_many_corners` (8-connected expansion is already used).\n\nRelevant code: https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/blob/main/nav2_theta_star_planner/src/theta_star.cpp\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!queue_.empty()) {\n  // ...\n  if (isGoal(*curr_data)) {\n    break;\n  }\n\n  resetParent(curr_data);\n  setNeighbors(curr_data);\n\n  curr_data = queue_.top();\n  queue_.pop();\n}\n\nif (queue_.empty()) {\n  raw_path.clear();\n  return false;\n}\n```\n\n## Minimal repro\n\nMap with two adjacent free cells. Start `(0,0)`, goal `(1,0)`. A 4-connected path exists.\n\nWith default weights (`w_euc_cost=1`, `w_traversal_cost=2`):\n\n1. `curr = start` (start is still in the queue)\n2. Expand start → goal is pushed\n3. Pop start again (`f(start) < f(goal)`)\n4. Expand start again, pop goal → queue is empty, `curr = goal`\n5. Loop exits because `queue_.empty()`\n6. `isGoal(goal)` is never checked → `return false`\n\nThe same false failure happens on a 2x2 map whose only connection is the diagonal (one 8-connected step).\n\nAn open 3x3 map often succeeds, because other open-set nodes remain when the goal is popped. That is why this is easy to miss in typical demos.\n\n## Real-world case\n\nOn a recorded global costmap, the robot was in a small 4-connected pocket (~147 cells). The only exit was one diagonal cell with cost 221 (both orthogonal neighbors were 253).\n\nThat gateway cell had a high traversal cost, so it was the last node popped from the open set and was never expanded. Theta* reported no path, even though an 8-connected path with cost `< 253` existed.\n\n## Expected\n\nPop a node, then test `isGoal` / run `setNeighbors`. An empty queue should mean “no node left to expand”, not “skip the node we just popped”.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nUse standard pop-then-expand:\n\n```cpp\nwhile (!queue_.empty()) {\n  tree_node * curr_data = queue_.top();\n  queue_.pop();\n\n  if (isGoal(*curr_data)) {\n    backtrace(raw_path, curr_data);\n    clearQueue();\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  resetParent(curr_data);\n  setNeighbors(curr_data);\n}\n\nraw_path.clear();\nreturn false;\n```\n\nWith this change, the two-cell map, the diagonal 2x2 map, a 3-cell corridor, and the recorded pocket costmap all find a path.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">ThetaStar::generatePath</code> expands <code class=\"notranslate\">curr_data</code> <strong>before</strong> popping the next node from the open set. The loop condition is <code class=\"notranslate\">!queue_.empty()</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">After the last remaining node is popped, the queue is empty, so the loop exits <strong>without</strong>:</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>calling <code class=\"notranslate\">setNeighbors</code> on that node</li>\n<li>checking <code class=\"notranslate\">isGoal</code> on that node</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If that node is the only 8-connected gateway out of a pocket, or is the goal itself, planning returns failure even though a collision-free grid path exists.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is independent of <code class=\"notranslate\">how_many_corners</code> (8-connected expansion is already used).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Relevant code: <a href=\"https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/blob/main/nav2_theta_star_planner/src/theta_star.cpp\">https://github.com/ros-navigation/navigation2/blob/main/nav2_theta_star_planner/src/theta_star.cpp</a></p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-c++ notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"while (!queue_.empty()) {\n  // ...\n  if (isGoal(*curr_data)) {\n    break;\n  }\n\n  resetParent(curr_data);\n  setNeighbors(curr_data);\n\n  curr_data = queue_.top();\n  queue_.pop();\n}\n\nif (queue_.empty()) {\n  raw_path.clear();\n  return false;\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">while</span> (!queue_.empty()) {\n  <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">//</span> ...</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> (<span class=\"pl-c1\">isGoal</span>(*curr_data)) {\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">break</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">resetParent</span>(curr_data);\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">setNeighbors</span>(curr_data);\n\n  curr_data = queue_.<span class=\"pl-c1\">top</span>();\n  queue_.<span class=\"pl-c1\">pop</span>();\n}\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> (queue_.empty()) {\n  raw_path.<span class=\"pl-c1\">clear</span>();\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>;\n}</pre></div>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Minimal repro</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Map with two adjacent free cells. Start <code class=\"notranslate\">(0,0)</code>, goal <code class=\"notranslate\">(1,0)</code>. A 4-connected path exists.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With default weights (<code class=\"notranslate\">w_euc_cost=1</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">w_traversal_cost=2</code>):</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">curr = start</code> (start is still in the queue)</li>\n<li>Expand start → goal is pushed</li>\n<li>Pop start again (<code class=\"notranslate\">f(start) &lt; f(goal)</code>)</li>\n<li>Expand start again, pop goal → queue is empty, <code class=\"notranslate\">curr = goal</code></li>\n<li>Loop exits because <code class=\"notranslate\">queue_.empty()</code></li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">isGoal(goal)</code> is never checked → <code class=\"notranslate\">return false</code></li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The same false failure happens on a 2x2 map whose only connection is the diagonal (one 8-connected step).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">An open 3x3 map often succeeds, because other open-set nodes remain when the goal is popped. That is why this is easy to miss in typical demos.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Real-world case</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On a recorded global costmap, the robot was in a small 4-connected pocket (~147 cells). The only exit was one diagonal cell with cost 221 (both orthogonal neighbors were 253).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">That gateway cell had a high traversal cost, so it was the last node popped from the open set and was never expanded. Theta* reported no path, even though an 8-connected path with cost <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt; 253</code> existed.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Expected</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Pop a node, then test <code class=\"notranslate\">isGoal</code> / run <code class=\"notranslate\">setNeighbors</code>. An empty queue should mean “no node left to expand”, not “skip the node we just popped”.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Suggested fix</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Use standard pop-then-expand:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-c++ notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"while (!queue_.empty()) {\n  tree_node * curr_data = queue_.top();\n  queue_.pop();\n\n  if (isGoal(*curr_data)) {\n    backtrace(raw_path, curr_data);\n    clearQueue();\n    return true;\n  }\n\n  resetParent(curr_data);\n  setNeighbors(curr_data);\n}\n\nraw_path.clear();\nreturn false;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">while</span> (!queue_.empty()) {\n  tree_node * curr_data = queue_.<span class=\"pl-c1\">top</span>();\n  queue_.<span class=\"pl-c1\">pop</span>();\n\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> (<span class=\"pl-c1\">isGoal</span>(*curr_data)) {\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">backtrace</span>(raw_path, curr_data);\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">clearQueue</span>();\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>;\n  }\n\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">resetParent</span>(curr_data);\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">setNeighbors</span>(curr_data);\n}\n\nraw_path.clear();\n<span class=\"pl-k\">return</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>;</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With this change, the two-cell map, the diagonal 2x2 map, a 3-cell corridor, and the recorded pocket costmap all find a path.</p>",
